1
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:06,660
This video introduces the improvement plan for JEI Math Grades D–I.

2
00:00:07,060 --> 00:00:12,320
We will explore the three key directions for improvement, the detailed changes for each grade,

3
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:15,080
and how the supplementary materials will be utilized.

4
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:22,370
Currently, approximately 80% of our total members are concentrated in Grades D–I.

5
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:26,840
Therefore, based on JEI’s unique and systematic learning structure,

6
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:29,940
we have selected these grades as our top priority for improvement,

7
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:35,230
with the goal of strengthening alignment with the Common Core State Standards (CCSS)

8
00:00:35,230 --> 00:00:37,360
and optimizing the learner experience.

9
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:43,810
The first area of improvement is to strengthen the incorporation of the CCSS.

10
00:00:44,210 --> 00:00:48,810
When comparing JEI’s learning sequence with the CCSS progression,

11
00:00:48,810 --> 00:00:51,880
the timing and progression of learning do not always align.

12
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:58,150
In particular, we will closely review the timing and progression of learning and CCSS alignment.

13
00:01:00,050 --> 00:01:03,100
Building on JEI’s systematic learning roadmap,

14
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:07,330
we aim to further enhance alignment with grade-level standards in the U.S.,

15
00:01:07,330 --> 00:01:10,230
maximizing both the timeliness and completeness of learning.

16
00:01:12,130 --> 00:01:18,040
For example, in Grade D, we have strengthened students’ understanding of the relational meaning of the equal sign,

17
00:01:18,040 --> 00:01:21,140
emphasizing that both sides represent equal quantities.

18
00:01:21,540 --> 00:01:24,350
We have also added word problems involving three numbers

19
00:01:24,350 --> 00:01:29,710
to further develop students’ ability to apply mathematical concepts to real-life situations.

20
00:01:31,610 --> 00:01:34,900
In Grade I, we have newly introduced the coordinate plane

21
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:39,730
and strengthened learning related to comparing integers and understanding absolute value,

22
00:01:39,730 --> 00:01:43,220
allowing students to progress naturally toward more advanced concepts.

23
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:51,160
Through these changes, we will connect JEI’s strong learning system more closely with the local curriculum

24
00:01:51,160 --> 00:01:54,880
and further strengthen the natural connections between concepts across grades.

25
00:01:57,480 --> 00:02:02,190
The second direction is to improve page structure based on the amount of learning content.

26
00:02:02,590 --> 00:02:06,950
The existing pages provided 12 to 24 calculation practice problems,

27
00:02:06,950 --> 00:02:10,770
offering students valuable opportunities for practice and mastery.

28
00:02:11,170 --> 00:02:15,570
However, to reduce learner fatigue and help students focus more deeply on concepts,

29
00:02:15,570 --> 00:02:18,210
we have reorganized the content more efficiently.

30
00:02:18,610 --> 00:02:24,780
Accordingly, the main textbook has been redesigned around conceptual understanding and representative problems,

31
00:02:24,780 --> 00:02:27,790
allowing students to focus on key learning objectives

32
00:02:27,790 --> 00:02:30,390
while providing sufficient space for solving problems.

33
00:02:33,190 --> 00:02:36,610
The repetitive practice problems reduced from the main textbook

34
00:02:36,610 --> 00:02:41,220
will be reorganized into supplementary materials customized for each set.

35
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:45,420
When students need additional practice after completing the main textbook,

36
00:02:45,420 --> 00:02:49,890
centers will be able to use these materials flexibly according to individual learning needs.

37
00:02:51,790 --> 00:02:55,770
This approach reduces unnecessary learning burden in the main textbook

38
00:02:55,770 --> 00:02:58,430
while still providing sufficient opportunities for mastery

39
00:02:58,430 --> 00:03:02,770
through supplementary materials directly connected to each target set,

40
00:03:02,770 --> 00:03:04,760
ultimately supporting mastery learning.

41
00:03:06,660 --> 00:03:11,770
The third direction is to strengthen the connection between prerequisite concepts and subsequent learning.

42
00:03:12,170 --> 00:03:17,690
Building on JEI’s strong conceptual structure, we have further subdivided the learning steps

43
00:03:17,690 --> 00:03:21,490
so that students can transition more easily to higher-level concepts

44
00:03:21,490 --> 00:03:24,310
such as equations, fractions, and decimals.

45
00:03:26,210 --> 00:03:32,330
In Grade F, we have designed the concept of equal partitioning to naturally lead into fraction notation.

46
00:03:32,730 --> 00:03:37,300
We have also introduced the use of variables progressively according to students’ grade levels

47
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:39,760
to support intuitive understanding of equations.

48
00:03:41,660 --> 00:03:45,490
In Grades G and H, we have strengthened the use of visual models,

49
00:03:45,490 --> 00:03:48,920
such as number lines, area models, and grouping models,

50
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:52,520
so that students can develop a more intuitive understanding of rounding

51
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:55,390
and the principles of multiplying and dividing fractions.

52
00:03:57,290 --> 00:04:01,750
Furthermore, in Grade I, these foundations are systematically extended

53
00:04:01,750 --> 00:04:07,810
so that relationships between two variables naturally progress from equations to tables and then to graphs.

54
00:04:10,410 --> 00:04:13,170
Along with the evolution of these learning objectives,

55
00:04:13,170 --> 00:04:16,720
we are also redesigning the diagnostic assessment and system data.

56
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:22,750
Based on the revised standards, the system will not only accurately identify each student’s starting point

57
00:04:22,750 --> 00:04:28,010
but also automatically connect the results to personalized supplementary-material recommendations.

58
00:04:28,410 --> 00:04:33,220
This will create a more complete learning cycle from diagnosis to prescription to learning.

59
00:04:35,620 --> 00:04:41,590
Through these improvements, 140 of the 221 existing sets will maintain their current structure,

60
00:04:41,590 --> 00:04:46,210
while 81 sets will be revised and enhanced and 5 new sets will be added.

61
00:04:49,010 --> 00:04:54,790
For each grade, we will comprehensively implement the main textbook revision, system data updates,

62
00:04:54,790 --> 00:04:58,810
and supplementary-material development as one integrated package.

63
00:05:01,210 --> 00:05:04,090
Through this improvement aligned with global standards,

64
00:05:04,090 --> 00:05:07,790
we aim to help students understand mathematical concepts more clearly

65
00:05:07,790 --> 00:05:10,670
and confidently extend their learning to the next level.

66
00:05:11,070 --> 00:05:11,590
Thank you.

